times: Among nurses and carers trusted on their ward (perhaps 1 adult in 30), a small ward or unit closing to save money comes to about 1 in 3 over a working life (estimate; small rehabilitation and cottage wards are often the first cut), set at 1 to 2 in 100 a year among them
likelier: a nurse of long standing, a small or country hospital, a lean health budget
rarer: a person outside care work, a large well-funded hospital
gap: 5-20
tone: trouble
