who: colleague
earth: the college is ending the evening classes you have taught for years, and your students ask what happens now
scene: For eleven years {N} has taught the evening class at the college: tired people after work, learning what they missed at school. The college says evening classes do not pay and will end in June. Twelve students sign a card asking {N} what happens now.
scene W: The evening class is the one door left open for people the day school failed. {N} cannot stand to see it shut.
scene U: Some of {Ns} best students came to the subject at forty. The college is losing more than it saves.
scene B: A course that ends a certificate can be sold. One that ends in a love of learning is harder to price.
scene R: {N} would teach the class on the pavement if it came to that.
scene G: {N} learned at an evening class too, from an old teacher who taught it until the week he died.
