# ---------------------------------------------------------------- life event: the credit union's bad year (pairs D5a)

== the queue at the credit union
tier: life event
sphere: comm
haunt: comm.credit
ladder: pillar
at: bank
stages: adult mature elder
age: 30-100
per_year: 0 0 0 .01 .015 .01
drivers: money-.3 unrest+.2
times: Among people trusted to sit on the board of a credit union, savings circle or co-op bank (perhaps 1 adult in 100), a bad loan and a rush of members taking their savings out comes to about 1 in 5 (estimate; runs on small lenders follow a loss made public, Diamond and Dybvig 1983), set at 1 in 100 a year among them
likelier: a long-serving board member, a small lender in a lean year, a town where word travels fast
rarer: a large bank, a lender with savings guaranteed by law
gap: 8-25
tone: trouble
life: money, community, work
horizon: months
roles: neighbour, friend, colleague, patron
who: neighbour
earth: the credit union you help run has lost money on a bad loan, members are queueing to take their savings out, and the board looks to you
scene: The town's credit union has lost money on one large loan gone bad, and members are queueing to take their savings out. {N} has sat on its board for years, and the others want {N} to take the chair and face the queue.
scene W: The members trusted the board with their savings. They are owed the truth, and the same answer each.
scene U: {N} has been through the books. The loss is real but not fatal, if the members stay.
scene B: Whoever stands in front of that queue will be remembered for it, one way or the other.
scene R: {N} feels the old pull: walk out to the queue and turn it round with a few words.
scene G: The credit union was started by the street's grandparents, a few coins a week each. It is the street's own.
