earth: your ward's councillor has moved away, nominations for the seat close on Friday, and three neighbours are at your door with a form
scene: The ward's councillor has moved away. Nominations for the by-election close on Friday at noon. So far only one name is in, from a man nobody on the estate has met. Three neighbours are at {Ns} door with a form, their signatures already on it.
scene W: Someone has to answer for the ward. {N} believes in doing a thing properly or not at all.
scene U: {N} knows the estate's troubles better than anyone, down to the numbers. Whether that makes a councillor is another question.
scene B: A seat on the council is a lever on everything: the repairs, the bus, the school. {N} has wanted one for years.
scene R: {Ns} heart is going. The form is right there, and Friday is three days away.
scene G: The estate has always had one of its own on the council. The man nobody has met is not one of its own.
